> There is a meaningful React Aria parity gap in the semantic API.
Base UI currently offers a lower-level surface: format, timezone, referenceDate, and for time/date-time, ampm and step. React Aria pairs its segmented model with semantic props like granularity, hourCycle, hideTimeZone, placeholderValue, and isDateUnavailable, plus an explicit DateInput container with its own state surface. Base UI’s token-level format is actually more powerful for exact layouts like EEEE, MMMM dd, yyyy or yyyy-MM-dd, but it also makes the component easier to misuse and much harder to document precisely. ([[GitHub](https://github.com/flaviendelangle/base-ui/raw/refs/heads/date-field-component/docs/src/app/%28docs%29/react/components/date-field/types.md)][5](https://github.com/flaviendelangle/base-ui/raw/refs/heads/date-field-component/docs/src/app/%28docs%29/react/components/date-field/types.md))

